Braille Support for the GRUB Boot Loader
==========================================

BRLTTY can run as a loadable GRUB module, providing braille display
accessibility during the boot menu. This allows blind users to read
and navigate the GRUB menu using a refreshable braille display.

Supported Braille Displays
--------------------------

All USB braille displays supported by BRLTTY should work. The braille display
must be connected through a USB 2.0 port (UHCI, OHCI, or EHCI controller).
USB 3.0 (xHCI) controllers are not currently supported by GRUB's USB stack.

Serial-attached braille displays are also supported via GRUB's serial port
driver.

Bluetooth braille displays are not supported — GRUB has no Bluetooth stack.

Speech output is not available — GRUB has no audio subsystem.

Building
--------

The module must be built against the GRUB source tree. There is no
``grub-devel`` package providing the required headers.

1. Obtain the GRUB source::

      git clone https://git.savannah.gnu.org/git/grub.git /path/to/grub

   Alternatively, use your distribution's GRUB source::

      dnf download --source grub2        # Fedora/RHEL
      apt-get source grub2               # Debian/Ubuntu

2. Create a symlink named ``grub-root`` in the BRLTTY source root pointing to
   the GRUB source tree::

      cd /path/to/brltty
      ln -s /path/to/grub grub-root

3. Configure the build::

      ./cfg-grub

   Additional configure options may be passed through::

      ./cfg-grub --with-braille-driver=hw

4. Build::

      make

Installation
------------

1. Copy ``brltty.mod`` to the GRUB modules directory::

      # EFI systems:
      cp brltty.mod /boot/grub/x86_64-efi/

      # Legacy BIOS systems:
      cp brltty.mod /boot/grub/i386-pc/

2. To load the module automatically at every boot, add the following to
   ``/etc/default/grub``::

      GRUB_PRELOAD_MODULES="usb uhci ohci ehci brltty"

   Then regenerate the GRUB configuration::

      grub-mkconfig -o /boot/grub/grub.cfg

   On some distributions this is done with::

      update-grub

Loading Manually
----------------

From the GRUB command line, load the USB stack and then the BRLTTY module::

   grub> insmod usb
   grub> insmod uhci
   grub> insmod ohci
   grub> insmod ehci
   grub> insmod brltty

For serial-attached displays, load the serial module instead::

   grub> insmod serial
   grub> insmod brltty

Troubleshooting
---------------

Display not detected
   Ensure the USB modules are loaded before ``brltty.mod``. The display must
   be plugged in before loading the module.

Only some USB ports work
   GRUB's USB stack supports UHCI, OHCI, and EHCI controllers only. Try
   different USB ports — many systems have a mix of USB 2.0 and 3.0 ports.

Limitations
-----------

* Bluetooth is not supported.
* Speech is not supported.
* USB 3.0 (xHCI) host controllers are not supported by GRUB.
* The module must be compiled from source against a GRUB source tree that
  matches (or is close to) the installed GRUB version.
